From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:09:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuttlefish: let a product keep ro.adb.secure of its build
 type

The user block of shared/device.mk adds ro.adb.secure=0 to the product
partition ("spawn adbd by default without authorization"). The product
build.prop is read after system's and system_ext's, so a product that
inherits it reads 0 on a user build whatever the build type says. A
product that has its own adb authorization policy still needs the build
type's value: Settings hides "Revoke USB debugging authorizations" while
the property is false, and the user could no longer revoke the
computers they allowed.

A product that sets UML_ANDROID_KEEP_ADB_SECURE to true now drops the
entry at the end of this file. Only the file that adds an entry can
remove it: inherit-product merges an inherited list after the product's
own entries, and the product property lists are read-only once the
product configuration has run, so neither the product makefile nor
BoardConfig.mk can. A product that does not set the switch is
unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 shared/device.mk | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/shared/device.mk b/shared/device.mk
index b173afba75dc3b61e0192970202e083a0c362ca6..65f8dfa2ddea9a7b4e1ea280be80382328799176 100644
--- a/shared/device.mk
+++ b/shared/device.mk
@@ -686,3 +686,16 @@ endif
 
 PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
     device_google_cuttlefish_shared_config_dma_heap_config
+
+# A product that keeps the build type's adb authorization (it sets
+# UML_ANDROID_KEEP_ADB_SECURE) does not get the user block's
+# ro.adb.secure=0: the product partition's build.prop is read after
+# system's and system_ext's ro.adb.secure=1, and Settings hides "Revoke
+# USB debugging authorizations" while the property is false. The filter
+# sits in this file because inherit-product merges an inherited list
+# after the product's own entries, so only the file that adds the entry
+# can remove it; the product property lists are read-only once the
+# product configuration has run.
+ifeq ($(UML_ANDROID_KEEP_ADB_SECURE),true)
+PRODUCT_PRODUCT_PROPERTIES := $(filter-out ro.adb.secure=%,$(PRODUCT_PRODUCT_PROPERTIES))
+endif
